      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1782102423186,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "dynamic blocks connected by any reference are live blocks.\nIn java garbage dynamic blocks are blocks which r not connected by any reference.\n\nGargage collector\n=================\n\nIt is an software under the control of jvm as a name indicates its job is to \ndeallocates garbage blocks from heap.\n\nThis means GC run and scans entire heap for garbage blocks and destorys them\n\nGC works in backgraound, and programmer doesn't know when deallocation accurs.\n\nThus programmer know allocation but not deallocation.\n\nGC is a lazy process , it happens when  when memory is required.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "dynamic blocks connected by any reference are live blocks.\nIn java garbage dynamic blocks are blocks which r not connected by any reference.\n\nGargage collector\n=================\n\nIt is an software under the control of jvm as a name indicates its job is to \ndeallocates garbage blocks from heap.\n\nThis means GC run and scans entire heap for garbage blocks and destorys them\n\nGC works in backgraound, and programmer doesn't know when deallocation accurs.\n\nThus programmer know allocation but not deallocation.\n\nGC is a lazy process , it happens when  when memory is required.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
